        "original_id": "1644df4f-6f41-549d-85d3-b1fcc1f0fec9",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Hannah Arendt\n- Works: The Origins of Totalitarianism\n- Concepts: Nazism, Stalinism, totalitarianism, political theory\n\nFacts:\n- Hannah Arendt was born on 14 October 1906 and died on 4 December 1975.\n- Hannah Arendt was a German-born American political theorist.\n- Hannah Arendt wrote The Origins of Totalitarianism.\n- The Origins of Totalitarianism was published in 1951.\n- The Origins of Totalitarianism is also known in German as \"Elemente und Ursprünge totaler Herrschaft\" and in English as \"Elements and Origins of Totalitarian Rule.\"\n- The Origins of Totalitarianism describes and analyzes Nazism and Stalinism.\n- The Origins of Totalitarianism treats Nazism and Stalinism as the major totalitarian political movements of the first half of the 20th century.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
